  "ingredients": [
    "2.25 cups all-purpose flour",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "0.25 teaspoon salt",
    "1 cup white sugar",
    "0.33333334326744 cup orange juice",
    "2 eggs",
    "1 cup buttermilk",
    "2 tablespoons cranberry-flavored liqueur",
    "0.75 cup vegetable oil",
    "1 cup chopped dates",
    "1 cup fresh cranberries",
    "2 tablespoons grated orange zest",
    "1 cup orange juice",
    "0.75 cup white sugar"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease and flour a 10 inch tube pan. Sift together the flour, baking soda, baking powder and salt; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/TSv6CRBiI3Ewh1NAbPqcfvfNVNE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-01-3a339699cb0b449da93188841cbed9d8.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl, mix together 1 cup of white sugar, 1/3 cup of orange juice, eggs, buttermilk, cranberry liqueur, and vegetable oil using an electric mixer.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/RpCSKkiPHoKFRIsmq1Z9Q7KrLP4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-02-53b422a3a82e48fba73976f4faceca7d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the dry ingredients and mix just until moistened. Fold in the chopped dates, cranberries and orange zest. Pour the batter into the prepared pan and spread evenly.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/c9oWtsuW1XsDAmZNSDHH-pA5yAY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-03-d66f8444c90247c1a6840ef403f2aa3e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 1 hour in the preheated oven, or until a knife inserted into the crown of the cake comes out clean. Let the cake cool in the pan set over a wire rack for 15 to 20 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sezeEjiIr41rKAr-NVgQnKzNGKs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-04-63a0aab7d7c84b23b7725d86f5a3a72d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove the cake from the pan and place on a serving plate. In a small saucepan, stir together 1 cup of orange juice and 3/4 cup of white sugar. Bring to a boil, stirring until the sugar has dissolved.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/93BZhD3tplE8lBuTgsqRRx-_ptw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-05-856a459512624bd2beaa736be190c9ee.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a turkey baster or large spoon to drizzle the sauce over the cake. Poke the cake with a fork or skewer to help it absorb all of the sauce, or until the cake is thoroughly moistened.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/PuiMsoJfCgZJflvroXsChDt10o8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/55378-grandmas-cranberry-orange-cake-VAT-step-06-c9883775694443ec92ab660bad4efdea.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/55378/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
